So it turns out my 85th game of nethack is my first ascension.  Yay
me!

I went to minetown first: it's dangerous, but the daggers, altar and
dwarvish mithril are too good to pass up.  I found a magic lamp in the
mines (another reason to head into minetown first), and when I got to
town the altar was coaligned, so I made some holy water and wished for
+3 blessed greased GDSM.  Since polytraps couldn't hurt me, I decided
to go on to mine's end, and was very nearly killed by a pack of fire
giants; I fell to 3 HP and prayed for help, which I got.  I also found
a second magic lamp!  I wished for the Master Key of thievery: that
1/2 physical damage is too good to pass up, and I knew I might not be
able to wish for it later (in a previous game, I wandered on a bones
file with Cleaver and the Heart of Ahrimann, ruining my ability to
wish for artifacts).

Sokoban had an amulet of reflection, so I dug past medusa, then went
backupstairs to kill her.  She had a shield of reflection. I went to
the castle, using the drawbridge to squish as much as I could.  I
found the wand and wished for scrolls of charging, bag of holding,
uncursed magic marker, speed boots, and amulet of life saving.  This
is farther than I'd ever gotten before in a game, so I was feeling
pretty good.  Then I stupidly fell into the trap to the Valley of the
Dead.  Without a source of levitation, I had to use my magic marker to
write a scroll of earth (I left the sokoban ones in a stash) to fill
in the holes so I could get back across.  Then I realized I still
needed a way to cross medusa's level.  Fortunately, Perseus's statue
had some cursed flying boots (and another polished shield!) for me.
If not for those, I'm not sure how I would have gotten back.

I collected my stuff, got Stormbringer as a sac gift, and laid with a
succubus to level 14.  Stormbringer+foocubus= level gain without level
drain, which is nice.  The quest was pretty easy, and I used my magic
marker to enchant the Longbow to +7, Stormbringer to +3, and my armor
until I was AC -26 before it dried up.  I tried my hand at polypiling,
which I'd never done before.  It didn't work as well as I'd hoped:
lot's of fusing, lots of useless junk, but I did get a ring of
conflict.  I  felt pretty equipped, so I descended into hell.  Vlad
gave me his candelabrum and another life saver.  I also found 3 more
life saving amulets loose in the dungeon, which made that wish feel a
little wasted, although I'm sure if I died before I got to Vlad I
wouldn't feel that way.  I did use one: I fell into a pit while
wielding a cockatrice corpse.  I found the vibrating square, then used
a pickaxe to dig straight lines from door to door all the way back to
level 1.  I'd never met Rodney before, but I hoped to make it quick.
I found another magic lamp in Gehenom, and I used it for a ring of
levitation, plus my wrest wish from the wand for 3 scrolls of gold
detection.

My plan for dealing with the Wizard and the Riders was the single wand
of death(0:2) I got from Orcus, plus my two remaining blessed scrolls
of charging.  But then I walked into the Wizard's moat without putting
my levitation ring on first, blanking most of my scrolls.  I went
ahead and zapped him, took the book, raced down, did the ritual, and
entered moloch's sanctum.  As I mentioned in a previous post, Yeenoghu
fetched the amulet for me, which was kind of nice.  Unfortunately, I
had a bad encounter with a mind flayer in the sanctum, causing me to
forget many of the hard-dug paths back up through the dungeon.  As I
wandered through mazes that "seemed familiar" I met rodney 4 more
times.  I used my last charge from my wand of death, then a
cockatrice, and then twice just beat him to death, a slow and painful
process, especially with double trouble (although Stormbringer's drain
helped).

I went up the last upstair, and into the plane of earth, killed Rodney
again, and decided to find this portal by hand, since I only had 3
gold scrolls.  Here the RNG did me one last favor: a monster was
carrying a wand of death (0:6)!  I found the portal, used a
combination of conflict, levitation, and gold scrolls to make quick
work of the next 3 planes, and entered astral.

I'd never been here before, so I wasn't quite sure what to expect.  As
it says in the spoilers, wands of teleport are nice to move the
millions of minions out of the way.  Killing things was pretty much
pointless, more would be summoned.  I ended up having to visit all 3
altars: my newfound wand made quick work of Pestilence and Famine, and
though death took me down to 85hp, it wasn't too bad in the end.  I
was made a demigod and jumped up and hugged my wife (who didn't
exactly share my enthusiasm, although she liked my happy dance).

So the first game where I made it into the castle was also my first
ascension, which does seem to say the first half of the game is harder
than the second.  I was never as close to dying as when I prayed for
help in the Mines.  I made liberal use of spoilers, without which I'm
sure I would have never ascended.  I can't deny that the RNG was
extremely good to me: 9 wishes, boots of levitation when I needed
them, wand of death when I needed it.  The real question in my mind
now is whether I could ascend without all that help.  But I think I'll
take a break before  I tackle the game again, and I may try a
different race.  I've always played orcs, a dwarf might be an
interesting change...

Oh and thanks to everyone at RGRN who answered my questions with with
good advice.  Really, any game is only as good as the community plays
and supports it, which is part of what makes nethack so interesting.
-Tom


